segments.source:
We can check that our solution is correct by substituting <m>(x,y,z)=(1,-2,3)</m> into the original equation:
      <me>
        \syseq{x + 2y + 3z = 6;
        2x - 3y + 2z = 14;
        3x + y - z = -2
        }
        \quad\xrightarrow{\text{substitute}}\quad
        \syseq{
        1 + 2\cdot(-2) + 3\cdot 3 = 6;
        2\cdot 1 - 3\cdot(-2) + 2\cdot 3 = 14;
        3\cdot 1 + (-2) - 3 = -2\rlap.
        }
      </me>

We can make our life easier by extracting only the numbers, and putting them in a box:
    <idx><h>Augmented matrix</h><see>Matrix</see></idx>
    <me>
      \syseq{x + 2y + 3z = 6;
      2x - 3y + 2z = 14;
      3x + y - z = -2
      }
      \quad\xrightarrow{\text{becomes}}\quad
      \amat{
      1  2  3  6 ;
      2  -3  2  14;
      3  1  -1  -2
      }.
    </me>

