Now we translate this augmented matrix back into a system of equations:
        <me>
          \amat{
          1  2  3  6 ;
          0 1 2 4 ;
          0 0 1 3
          } \quad\xrightarrow{\text{becomes}}\quad
          \syseq{
          x + 2y + 3z = 6;
          \. \+ y + 2z = 4;
          \. \+ \. \+ z = 3}
        </me>
        Hence <m>z=3</m>; back-substituting as in this <xref ref="systems-eqns-example1"/> gives <m>(x,y,z)=(1,-2,3)</m>.

segments.translation:
이제 이 첨가행렬을 다시 연립방정식으로 옮깁니다: <me>
          \amat{
