segments.source:
For example,
        <me>
          \amat{
          1  2  3  6 ;
          0 1 2 4 ;
          0 0 10 30
          } \quad\xrightarrow{\text{becomes}}\quad
          \syseq{
          x + 2y + 3z = 6;
          \. \+ y + 2z = 4;
          \. \+ \. \+ 10z = 30\rlap.}
        </me>
        We immediately see that <m>z=3</m>, which implies <m>y = 4-2\cdot 3 = -2</m> and <m>x = 6 - 2(-2) - 3\cdot 3 = 1.</m>

