This results in the system of equations:
        <me>
          \syseq{x - y = 0;
          \.  \+ y = 1\rlap.
          }
        </me>
	In terms of row operations on matrices, we can write this as:
          <me>\def\r{\color{red}}
            \begin{split}
            \amat{1 -1 0; 1 1 2}
            \quad\xrightarrow{R_2=R_2-R_1}\quad&amp;
            \amat{1 -1 0; 0 2 2} \\
            \quad\xrightarrow{R_2=\frac{1}{2}R_2}\quad&amp;
            \amat{1 -1 0; 0 1 1}
            \end{split}
          </me>
          <latex-code><![CDATA[
